  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ukraine Road Corridors</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of a sovereign loan of up to EUR 450 million to Ukraine to be on-lent  to the State Agency for Restoration and Development of Infrastructure of  Ukraine, formerly known as the State Road Agency of Ukraine or Ukravtodor (the  &quot;Agency&quot; or the &quot;Client&quot;), consisting of three tranches (the &quot;Project&quot;):    * Tranche 1 of up to EUR 183 million to finance the capital repair of M-09  Ternopil - Lviv - Rava-Ruska road section between Lviv and Rava-Ruska;   * Tranche 2 of up to EUR 160 million and Tranche 3 of up to EUR 107 million  to finance the restoration of operational condition and safety improvements on  the sections of M-06 Kyiv-Chop road in Kyiv, Zhytomyr and Rivne regions.  Tranche 1 will support the capital repair of the M-09 Ternopil - Lviv -  Rava-Ruska road section between Lviv and Rava-Ruska on the Polish-Ukrainian  border. Tranches 2 and 3 will support the restoration of operational condition  and safety improvements on the sections of M-06 Kyiv-Chop road in Kyiv,  Zhytomyr and Rivne regions. The ongoing war on Ukraine has prompted a  re-assessment of priorities following the redirection of traffic to the land  routes connecting Ukraine to the EU. The Project will enable critical road  infrastructure repairs on the road links that are part of the TEN-T corridor  network and will address the immediate priorities of developing alternative  transport routes to facilitate export and import logistics in line with the  EU-Ukraine Solidarity Lanes initiative and in response to the war on Ukraine.  The Project will also support legal and regulatory reform objectives aimed at  developing a competitive and transparent road construction and maintenance  sector.</narrative>
  </description>
